  "rhythm": "User-supplied MIDI file (99b18bab-totally_original_song_I_made_myself.mid, 123 BPM, 4/4 assumed, no time-signature event): lead track (muted-trumpet program, channel 0) from the very first note through the A4 at beat 64 (about 31.2 s of the original at 123 BPM), four 16-beat statements of the theme. Onsets are taken straight from the MIDI and written onset to next onset (the file's notes are slightly detached). Statements 1 and 3 hold the C#5 into a closing B4; in 2 and 4 the C#5 is held and the line then rests (4.25 beats), as in the file. The final A4 (the next statement's first note) is cut to 2 beats so the piece ends on the tonic: 66 beats, 32.2 s, so max_seconds is raised to 33. Only one source: no second transcription to check the melody against. Band, all from the same MIDI and moved -7 like the melody, beats counted from the first ocarina note: drums = the file's drum track for beats 0-66 (keys 24 and 41 on the beats, plus its fill before beat 32; 24 is not a GM key so it is written as kick 36, 41 kept as the low tom), drums alone for 4 beats first; from beat 32 (where the file's band enters) bass = the contrabass track's root on each beat (offbeat octave jumps left out), an octave up; trumpet part = the second muted-trumpet track (counter line), an octave up; strings = the file's held E5 drone, down an octave, split into notes of at most 16 beats. Quiet closed hats (key 42) added where the lead or the trumpet line plays between beats so every band onset lands on a drum hit. Shortest note is an eighth (0.24 s), no slow-down."
